1
00:00:00,460 --> 00:00:05,956
A useful school AI pilot should reduce repeated work without reducing
teacher control.

2
00:00:07,036 --> 00:00:15,100
EdulabsAI connects curriculum-aware planning, editable resources, live
delivery, evidence and the next teaching decision.

3
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:23,764
Teachers can work across broad K–12 curricula and subjects, with
optional source grounding for exact local material.

4
00:00:24,844 --> 00:00:32,020
Class and group communication is teacher administered, moderated and
paused during focused assessments when required.

5
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:39,748
Paper recognition is de-identified and review-first, so automation never
silently becomes a grade.

6
00:00:40,828 --> 00:00:46,636
Family communication is consent first, source backed and teacher
approved before delivery.

7
00:00:47,716 --> 00:00:55,012
The result is one inspectable lesson record with clear human
checkpoints, instead of scattered tools and copied context.

8
00:00:56,092 --> 00:01:00,196
Book an EdulabsAI school pilot at edulabsai dot com.

